\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Stevland Hardaway Morris
\f1\b0 \'a0({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:IPA/English"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 /\uc0\u712 sti\u720 v\u716 l\u601 nd/}};\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Birth_name#Maiden_and_married_names"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 n\'e9}}\'a0
\f0\b Judkins
\f1\b0 ; born May 13, 1950), known professionally as\'a0
\f0\b Stevie Wonder
\f1\b0 , is an American-Ghanaian singer-songwriter, musician, and record producer. He is regarded as one of the most influential musicians of the 20th century. Wonder is credited as a pioneer and influence by musicians across a range of genres that include\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhythm_and_blues"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 R&B}},\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pop_music"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 pop}},\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soul_music"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 soul}},\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gospel_music"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 gospel}},\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Funk"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 funk}}, and\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jazz"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 jazz}}. A virtual\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One-man_band"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 one-man band}}, Wonder's use of\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Synthesizer"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 synthesizers}}\'a0and other\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electronic_musical_instrument"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 electronic musical instruments}}\'a0during the 1970s reshaped the conventions of\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contemporary_R%26B"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 contemporary R&B}}. He also helped drive such genres into the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Album_era"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 album era}}, crafting his\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LP_record"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 LPs}}\'a0as cohesive and consistent, in addition to socially conscious statements with complex compositions.\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Visual_impairment"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Blind}}\'a0since shortly after his birth, Wonder was a\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Child_prodigy"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 child prodigy}}\'a0who signed with\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Motown"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Motown}}'s\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tamla"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Tamla}}\'a0label at the age of 11, where he was given the professional name\'a0
\f0\b Little Stevie Wonder
\f1\b0 .\
Wonder's single "{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fingertips"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Fingertips}}" was a No. 1 hit on the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Hot_100"}}{\fldrslt 
\f2\i \cf4 \strokec4 Billboard
\f1\i0 \'a0Hot 100}}\'a0in 1963, when he was 13, making him the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Billboard_Hot_100_chart_achievements_and_milestones#Age_records"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 youngest solo artist ever}}\'a0to top the chart. Wonder's critical success was at its peak in the 1970s. His "classic period" began in 1972 with the releases of\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_My_Mind"}}{\fldrslt 
\f2\i \cf4 \strokec4 Music of My Mind}}\'a0and\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talking_Book"}}{\fldrslt 
\f2\i \cf4 \strokec4 Talking Book}}, the latter featuring "{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superstition_(song)"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Superstition}}", which is one of the most distinctive and famous examples of the sound of the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clavinet"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Hohner Clavinet}}\'a0keyboard. His works\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Innervisions"}}{\fldrslt 
\f2\i \cf4 \strokec4 Innervisions}}\'a0(1973),\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fulfillingness%27_First_Finale"}}{\fldrslt 
\f2\i \cf4 \strokec4 Fulfillingness' First Finale}}\'a0(1974) and\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Songs_in_the_Key_of_Life"}}{\fldrslt 
\f2\i \cf4 \strokec4 Songs in the Key of Life}}\'a0(1976) all won the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammy_Award_for_Album_of_the_Year"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Grammy Award for Album of the Year}}, making him the only artist to have won the award with three consecutive album releases. Wonder began his "commercial period" in the 1980s; he achieved his biggest hits and highest level of fame, had increased album sales, charity participation, high-profile collaborations (including with\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_McCartney"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Paul McCartney}}\'a0and\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Jackson"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Michael Jackson}}), political impact, and television appearances. Wonder has continued to remain active in music and political causes.\
Wonder is one of the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_best-selling_music_artists"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 best-selling music artists of all time}}, with sales of over 100 million records worldwide. He has won 25\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grammy_Awards"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Grammy Awards}}\'a0(the most by a male solo artist) and one\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Academy_Awards"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Academy Award}}\'a0({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Academy_Award_for_Best_Song"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Best Original Song}}, for the 1984 film\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Woman_in_Red_(1984_film)"}}{\fldrslt 
\f2\i \cf4 \strokec4 The Woman in Red}}). Wonder has been inducted into the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhythm_and_Blues_Music_Hall_of_Fame"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Rhythm and Blues Music Hall of Fame}}, the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_and_Roll_Hall_of_Fame"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Rock and Roll Hall of Fame}}\'a0and the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Songwriters_Hall_of_Fame"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Songwriters Hall of Fame}}. He is also noted for his political activism, including his 1980 campaign to make\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martin_Luther_King_Jr."}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Martin Luther King Jr.}}'s birthday a\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martin_Luther_King_Jr._Day"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 federal holiday}}\'a0in the United States. In 2009, Wonder was named a\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations_Messengers_of_Peace"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 United Nations Messenger of Peace}}, and in 2014, he was honored with the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Presidential_Medal_of_Freedom"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Presidential Medal of Freedom}}.\
