\cf2 Wonder was born Stevland Hardaway Judkins in\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saginaw,_Michigan"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Saginaw, Michigan}}, on May 13, 1950, the third of five children born to\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lula_Mae_Hardaway"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Lula Mae Hardaway}},{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stevie_Wonder#cite_note-blindfaith-6"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs25\fsmilli12800 \cf4 \super \strokec4 [6]}}\'a0and the second of Hardaway's two children with Calvin Judkins.{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stevie_Wonder#cite_note-Ribowski-7"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs25\fsmilli12800 \cf4 \super \strokec4 [7]}}\'a0Wonder was born six weeks premature, a condition that, along with the oxygen-rich atmosphere in the hospital incubator, resulted in\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Retinopathy_of_prematurity"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 retinopathy of prematurity}}, a disease that aborts eye growth and often causes the\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Retina"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 retinas}}\'a0to detach, which left him blind.{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stevie_Wonder#cite_note-incubator-8"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs25\fsmilli12800 \cf4 \super \strokec4 [8]}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stevie_Wonder#cite_note-9"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs25\fsmilli12800 \cf4 \super \strokec4 [9]}}\
When Wonder was four, his mother divorced his father and moved with her three children to\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Detroit"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Detroit}}. Wonder attended Whitestone\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baptist"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Baptist}}\'a0Church, where he sang in the choir and became a\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solo_(music)"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 soloist}}\'a0at age eight.{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stevie_Wonder#cite_note-10"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs25\fsmilli12800 \cf4 \super \strokec4 [10]}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stevie_Wonder#cite_note-11"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs25\fsmilli12800 \cf4 \super \strokec4 [11]}}\'a0His mother later rekindled her relationship with her first child's father (whose surname was also coincidentally Hardaway),{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stevie_Wonder#cite_note-Ribowski-7"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs25\fsmilli12800 \cf4 \super \strokec4 [7]}}\'a0changed her name back to Lula Hardaway, and had two more children.\
Wonder began playing instruments at an early age, including piano, harmonica, and drums. He formed a singing partnership with a friend; calling themselves Stevie and John, they played on street corners and occasionally at parties and dances.{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stevie_Wonder#cite_note-12"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs25\fsmilli12800 \cf4 \super \strokec4 [12]}}\'a0When Stevie was signed by\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Motown"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Motown}}\'a0in 1961, his surname was legally changed to Morris, which (according to Lula Mae Hardaway's authorized biography) was an old family name.\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berry_Gordy"}}{\fldrslt \cf4 \strokec4 Berry Gordy}}\'a0was responsible for creating the stage name of "Little Stevie Wonder".{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stevie_Wonder#cite_note-13"}}{\fldrslt 
\fs25\fsmilli12800 \cf4 \super \strokec4 [13]}}\
Wonder attended Fitzgerald Elementary School in Detroit.{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stevie_Wonder#cite_note-14"}}{\fldrslt 
